.TH HD-LAUNCHER 8 "October 2026" "hd-desktop" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-launcher \- write the menu of the application launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-launcher
.RB [ \-n | \-\-dry\-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-launcher
writes the menu of the application launcher of the HyprDebian desktop,
.IR /var/cache/hd-launcher/launcher.json ,
the input of
.BR hd-menu (1),
from the
.I .desktop
files in
.I /usr/share/applications
and its subdirectories.
.PP
An application is in the menu when its
.I .desktop
file is of the
.B Type
Application, has a
.B Name
and an
.BR Exec ,
is not
.B NoDisplay
or
.BR Hidden ,
is not left out for Hyprland by
.B OnlyShowIn
or
.BR NotShowIn ,
has its
.B TryExec
installed, when it has one, and is not in the exclusion list.
.PP
The menu is 40% of the width and the height of the output; the options that
do not fit scroll.
Every application is an option: its
.B Name
is the label and its desktop file ID the value, such as
.IR firefox.desktop ;
the ID of a file in a subdirectory is its path below
.I /usr/share/applications
with \- for /.
A launcher starts it with
.BR "uwsm app \-\- <ID>" .
The options are sorted on the
.BR Name ,
in ascending order, without regard to case.
.PP
The icon of an application is looked up by its
.B Icon
in the icon themes hicolor and Adwaita and in
.IR /usr/share/pixmaps ,
or taken from its path when it is one.
A PNG is used as it is.
An SVG is rendered to a PNG of the
.B icon_size
of the
.B hd-theme
of
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
64 without one, in
.IR /var/cache/hd-launcher/icons ;
only when the PNG there was not rendered from that SVG at that size.
The icons of applications that are gone or left out are removed.
.PP
The apt hook
.I /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/90hd-launcher
runs
.B hd-launcher
each time apt has run dpkg: after an installation, an upgrade or a removal.
A failure is reported but does not fail apt.
The installation of
.BR hd-desktop (7)
runs it too.
After another theme is selected, with another
.BR icon_size ,
run it again.
.PP
Run it as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ,\  \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-n ,\  \-\-dry\-run
Print the menu that would be written, write nothing; it may be run by any
user.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The key
.B hd-launcher
of
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
is a list of the desktop file IDs to leave out of the menu; the
.I .desktop
at the end may be left out:
.PP
.RS
.nf
"hd-launcher": ["org.gnome.Meld.desktop", "debian-xterm"]
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/cache/hd-launcher/launcher.json
The menu, for
.BR hd-menu (1).
.TP
.I /var/cache/hd-launcher/icons
The PNGs rendered from SVG icons.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/90hd-launcher
The apt hook.
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The exclusion list, in the key
.BR hd-launcher ,
and the
.BR icon_size ,
in the key
.BR hd-theme .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the menu was written, 1 on an error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-desktop (7),
.BR hd-menu (1),
.BR hd-theme (7),
.BR hd-config (7)
